window.EF_CRUX_DOC_PAGES=["CH.52 — MODERN HISTORY: MISCELLANEOUS — FULL MIND MAP\n📋\nTopic-wise · Fully Explained · Hinglish · SSC / BPSC / BSSC / Railway\n Topics in this chapter:\n📑\n1. Early Colonial Administration & Governance Attitudes\n2. Anglo-Afghan Relations — Fear of Russia\n3. Match Lists — Anglo Wars & Treaties Dates\n4. A Disputed Match — Multiple Pairs\n5. Famines of the 19th Century\n6. Colonial Commissions & Their Chairmen\n7. Chronology — Early 19th Century Events\n8. Chronologically Last Events — Moplah Revolt\n9. Queen Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom\n10. Chronology — Press & Land Acts\n11. Match List — Social Reformers\n12. Disputed — 1857 Leaders & Ghadar Party\n13. The First Indian Cinema Advertisement\n14. Attlee's Statement on the Partition\n15. Famous Quotes on Freedom\n16. Chronology — Press & Societies Founding\n17. William A.J. Archibald\n18. Annie Besant's 'Tom-Tom' Statement\n19. Gandhi's Statement on Communal Differences\n20. Gandhi & Tilak — Social Regeneration\n21. Lala Lajpat Rai — Later Political Life\n22. G.V. Mavlankar — First to Discard the Official Wig\n23. World's First Woman PM & 10 Downing Street\n24. J.B. Kripalani's Kisan Mazdoor Praja Party\n25. Dr. Ambedkar's Death\n26. Rabindranath Tagore — 'Gurudev', Death & Views\n27. Ras Behari Bose's Rallying Statement\n28. 'Jai Jawan Jai Kisan' — Lal Bahadur Shastri\n29. The Gregorian Calendar\n30. Bhartiya Kisan Sangh\n31. Gandhi's Quit India Quotes\n32. Subhash Bose on Gandhi's Leadership\n33. Assertion-Reason — Nationalist Leaders & 'Providence'\n34. Nehru's Statement on Agriculture\n35. The First Cloth Mill in Bombay\n36. Dadabhai Naoroji's Statement\n37. Boy Scouts Movement — Baden-Powell\n38. The Rakhmabai Case (1884)\n39. Freedom Struggle — Incorrect Statement Check\n40. Statements About Jawaharlal Nehru — All Incorrect\n41. Nehru's Socialist-Republican Statement\n42. Nehru — 'High Priest of Communism' & His Biographer\n43. Ambabai — Woman Freedom Fighter\n44. The 'Sarabandi Campaign' — Sardar Patel\n45. The Origin of the Word 'Boycott'\n46. N.M. Joshi — India at the ILO\n47. Statements — Arya Samaj, Al-Hilal & Presidency College\n48. Chronology — 'Kesari' to 'Al Hilal'\n49. Third Event in Chronological Order — Dandi March\n50. Statements — Gandhi & Colonial Rule\n51. Aruna Asaf Ali's Post-1947 Contribution\n52. Sardar Patel's Statement on Bihar Riots\n53. First Demand for 'Complete Independence' — Hasrat Mohani\n54. Mountbatten on Jinnah's Role in Partition\n55. Aga Khan — The All Parties Muslim Conference","56. The Hindu Mahasabha — Banaras Session (1923)\n57. Sachchidananda Sinha — 'Creator of Modern Bihar'\n58. Founding Years — CPI & RSS (1925)\n59. 'Frontier Gandhi' — Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan\n60. The 'Bombay Trimurti'\n61. Khudai Khidmatgars — The 'Red Shirts'\n62. Dr. B.S. Moonje's Attack on Ambedkar\n63. History's Role in Creating Nationalism\n64. Tripura & the Freedom Movement\n65. Rajendra Prasad — From Bihar\n66. Women Saint Daya Bai\n67. St. Francis Xavier\n68. Jagat Narain Lal — Hazaribagh Jail\n69. The Aga Khan Palace Samadhis\n70. The Official History of Congress — Pattabhi Sitaramayya\n71. The Whitley Commission\n72. Foreign Commentators on Colonial India\n73. The Bengal Famine of 1943\n74. Non-Alignment\n75. Goa — Under Portuguese Control After Independence\n76. Nehru — NOT Influenced by German Nationalism\n77. Dominant Castes in Pre-Independence Bihar\n78. Shimla Conference & the Royal Indian Navy Revolt\n79. Statements — Vidyasagar & Bethune School\n80. Earliest Event — Neeldarpan\n81. First Indian in the British Parliament\n82. The Deoband Scholar — Abul Kalam Azad\n83. Chronology — Jallianwala Report to the Calcutta Session (1920)\n84. Independent India's First Industrial Policy\n85. The First Communist Government — Kerala\n86. National Observance Days\n87. Chronology — Air India to Goa (Post-Independence)\n88. Nehru vs Gandhi — Heavy Industrialization\n89. Gandhi's Statement at the Karachi Session (1931)\n90. The 'Struggle-Truce-Struggle' (S-T-S) Strategy\n91. The C.R. Formula\n92. Disputed — Organizations' Founding Years\n93. Gandhi's Key Milestones — Match List\n94. Chronology — Constitutional Reforms & Acts\n95. Chronology — Early Movements (1905-1916)\n96. Chronology — Rowlatt to Jallianwala Bagh (Multiple Sequences)\n97. Chronology — Lahore Session, Communal Award & Poona Pact\n98. Chronology — August Offer to Cabinet Mission (1940-1946)\n99. Match Lists — Movements & Their Leaders/Founders\n100. Match Lists & Not-Correctly-Matched Traps — Various Pairs\n101. The Trade Disputes Act, 1929\n102. Nehru's Political Career — Terms & Statements\n103. Quotes — Attlee, Cripps\n104. World History — Atomic Bomb & French Revolution\n105. Disputed Match — Pact/Year & Place\n106. Post-Independence Foreign Affairs Chronology\n107. The Shimla Agreement (1972)\n108. 'Operation Vijay' — Kargil War\n109. Kisan Diwas\n110. Nobel Prize Winners — Match List\n111. World Political Events — 20th Century\n112. World Leaders — Firsts & Notable Figures\n113. World History — Paper, Philosophy & the Renaissance\n114. The 'Kallar' Rebels of Madurai\n115. The Indian Councils Act of 1909\n116. Rama Devi — The Bijolia Peasant Movement\n117. Political Party Founding Years — Match List\n118. The 'Imperial Gazetteer' — W.W. Hunter","119. Gandhi & the Term 'Panchayati Raj'\n120. The Indian National Calendar\n121. Additional Committees, Chronology & Facts\n1. Early Colonial Administration & Governance Attitudes\n● Statement check: Lord Cornwallis pehle Governor-General the jinhone British pattern par regular police\nforce establish ki (statement 1 galat, unhone ki thi). Regulating Act 1773 ne Supreme Court banayi\n(sahi). IPC 1860 mein pehle Law Commission ki recommendations par draft hui (sahi). [Q1]\n● 'Paternalism in Governance' (patriarchal approach) India ke context mein British administrators jaise Sir\nThomas Munro se associate hai. [Q7]\n2. Anglo-Afghan Relations — Fear of Russia\n● 19th century mein Anglo-Afghan relations Russia ke India ki taraf expansion ke dar se influenced thi —\n1828 ke Treaty of Turkmenchay (Russia-Iran) ke baad, British ko Khyber-Bolan Passes ke through\nRussian invasion ka dar tha. [Q2]\n3. Match Lists — Anglo Wars & Treaties Dates\n● Match: First Anglo-Maratha War (1775-82); Second Anglo-Mysore War (1780-84); First Anglo-Burmese\nWar (1824-26); First Anglo-Afghan War (1839-42). [Q3]\n● Match: Second Anglo-Mysore War (1780-84); Second Anglo-French War (1750-54); Second Anglo-\nMaratha War (1803-05); Second Anglo-Afghan War (1878-80). [Q4]\n● Match: Treaty of Allahabad (1765); Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle (1748); La Bourdonnais' capture of Madras\n(1746); Dupleix's dismissal (1754). [Q5]\n● Sahi matched pairs: Third Anglo-Mysore War (1790-92) aur First Anglo-Burmese War (1824-26) —\n\n⚠️\nFirst Anglo-Maratha War 1775-82 mein thi (1767-69 mein nahi), aur Second Sikh War 1848-49 mein thi.\n[Q11]\n4. A Disputed Match — Multiple Pairs\n●\n Disputed: Farrukhsiyar ne Jizya tax dobara lagayi, British ne 1759 mein Masulipatnam par Colonel\n⚠️\nFrancis Ford ke through kabza kiya, Malcolm ka naam slavery ke end se associate NAHI hai, aur Sati\nPrevention Act ki jagah 'Bengal Sati Regulation (1829)' hona chahiye tha — multiple errors ki wajah se\nye question disputed hai. [Q6]\n5. Famines of the 19th Century\n● Orissa Famine (1866-67) ko 'Sea of Calamity' kaha gaya — Odisha mein akele 1.3 million log (aabadi\nka tihai) starvation-diseases se mare. [Q8]","● 'Indian Famine Code, 1883' Strachey Commission ne prepare ki — ye 1878 mein Great Famine (1876-\n78) ke baad famine-prevention measures ke liye appoint hui thi. [Q9]\n6. Colonial Commissions & Their Chairmen\n● Match: Andrew Fraser → Police Commission (1902-03); Antony MacDonell → Famine Commission\n(1900-01); Colin Scott Moncrieff → Irrigation Commission (1901-03); Thomas Robertson → Railway\nCommission (1901-03). [Q10, Q125]\n7. Chronology — Early 19th Century Events\n● Chronological order: Nana Phadnavis ki death (March 1800) → Wellesley ki recall (1805) → Vellore\nMutiny (10 July 1806) → Anglo-Nepalese War (1814-16). [Q12]\n● Battles ka chronological order: Battle of Shakarkheda (1724) → Battle of Bedara (1759) → Battle of\nPorto Novo (1781) → Battle of Mudki (1845). [Q13]\n8. Chronologically Last Events — Moplah Revolt\n● Chronologically aakhri event: Home Rule Movement (1916) → Jallianwala Bagh (13 April 1919) →\nKhilafat Movement (1919-24) → Moplah Revolt (1921). [Q14]\n9. Queen Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom\n● Queen Elizabeth II ne 70 saal reign kiya (1952-2022) aur 96 saal ki age mein (1926-2022) unki mrityu\nhui. [Q15]\n10. Chronology — Press & Land Acts\n● Chronological order: Dramatic Performance Act (1876) → Vernacular Press Act (1878) → Bengal\nTenancy Act (1885) → North-Western Provinces & Oudh Act (1890). [Q16]\n11. Match List — Social Reformers\n● Match: Child Marriage (against) → M.G. Ranade; Thuggee ka suppression → Colonel Sleeman; Widow\nRemarriage ka concept → Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar; Pindaris ka suppression → Lord Hastings. [Q17]\n12. Disputed — 1857 Leaders & Ghadar Party","●\n Disputed: Kunwar Singh (Bihar) aur Khan Bahadur Khan (Bareilly) ke baare mein statements sahi\n⚠️\nhain — lekin Maulvi Ahmadullah Faizabad mein lead karte the (Zeenat Mahal mein NAHI), aur Ghadar\nParty 1913 mein Lala Hardayal-Sohan Singh Bhakna ne banayi thi (Bhagat Singh ne NAHI) — isliye ye\nquestion disputed hai. [Q18]\n13. The First Indian Cinema Advertisement\n● 7 July 1896 ko, 'The Times of India' (Bombay) mein, Indian cinema ka pehla advertisement publish hua\n— usi din Lumiere brothers ne Watson's Hotel, Bombay mein pehla cinematography show diya. [Q19]\n14. Attlee's Statement on the Partition\n● 'British Government partition of India ke liye responsible nahi hai' — ye statement Lord Attlee ne diya\ntha, 20 February 1947 ko, power transfer ke baare mein. [Q20]\n15. Famous Quotes on Freedom\n● 'Political Freedom is the life-breath of a nation' — Aurobindo Ghosh ne kaha tha. [Q21]\n● Jayaprakash Narayan ne India mein 'Party Less Democracy' ka proposal diya tha. [Q22]\n● 'They both fought and collaborated with imperialism' — ye statement Rajani Palme Dutt ne Indian\nNational Congress ke baare mein kaha tha. [Q23]\n● 'New Lamps for Old' (1893-94) Aurobindo Ghosh ne likhi thi — apne Cambridge friend K.G. Deshpande\nke request par, 'Induprakash' weekly ke liye — Congress ko out-of-touch bataate hue. [Q24]\n16. Chronology — Press & Societies Founding\n● Chronological order: Hicky's 'Bengal Gazette' (1780) → Bengal Asiatic Society (1784) → Servants of\nIndia Society (1905) → Gadar Party (1913). [Q25]\n17. William A.J. Archibald\n●\n Trap: William A.J. Archibald, Lahore College ke Principal NAHI the — wo M.A.O. College (1905-\n⚠️\n1909), Government College Dhaka aur Muir Central College ke principal rahe. [Q26]\n18. Annie Besant's 'Tom-Tom' Statement\n● 'I am an Indian Tom-Tom, whose work is waking up all the sleepers' — ye statement Annie Besant ne\ndiya tha. [Q27]","19. Gandhi's Statement on Communal Differences\n●\n Multiple Correct: 'Jab tak British power yaha hai, hamare communal differences hume pareshaan\n⚠️\nkarte rahenge' — ye statement Mahatma Gandhi ne, American journalist Louis Fischer ko interview\nmein diya tha — options mein Gandhi na hone ki wajah se 'None of the above' sahi answer hai. [Q28]\n20. Gandhi & Tilak — Social Regeneration\n● Gandhi aur Tilak — dono ne social development ke liye India ka bahut travel kiya — Tilak pehle national\nleader the jinhone masses se close relationship banayi, Gandhi se pehle. [Q29]\n21. Lala Lajpat Rai — Later Political Life\n● Statement check: Lala Lajpat Rai shuru mein Non-cooperation ke favour mein nahi the, baad mein\nCalcutta Special Session (Sep 1920) mein iski resolution pass hone par ise support kiya — unhone C.R.\nDas-Motilal Nehru ki Swaraj Party bhi 1923 mein join ki, 1925 mein chhod di — dono statements sahi\nhain. [Q30]\n22. G.V. Mavlankar — First to Discard the Official Wig\n● G.V. Mavlankar, 1946 mein Central Legislative Assembly ke President bane — unhone mandatory wig\nhataakar Gandhi cap pehankar preside kiya. Wo pehle Lok Sabha Speaker bhi bane. [Q31]\n23. World's First Woman PM & 10 Downing Street\n● Duniya ki pehli lady Prime Minister Sirimavo Bhandaranaike (Sri Lanka) thi — July 1960 mein. [Q32]\n● '10 Downing Street' British Prime Minister ka official residence hai — Westminster mein situated. [Q33]\n24. J.B. Kripalani's Kisan Mazdoor Praja Party\n● Statement check: J.B. Kripalani ne 'Kisan Mazdoor Praja Party' 1951 mein banayi thi (1952 mein NAHI,\nstatement (i) galat) — 1952 mein ye Socialist Party ke saath merge hui. P.C. Ghosh aur T. Prakasam is\nparty se associate the (statement (ii) sahi). [Q34]\n25. Dr. Ambedkar's Death\n● Constitution ke maker Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ki mrityu 6 December 1956 ko New Delhi mein hui — unhe\n1990 mein posthumously Bharat Ratna mila. [Q35]","26. Rabindranath Tagore — 'Gurudev', Death & Views\n● Rabindranath Tagore ko 'Gurudev' kehte hain — unhone 'Gitanjali' ke liye 1913 mein Nobel Prize jeeta.\nUnki mrityu 7 August 1941 ko, Calcutta ke ancestral home mein hui. [Q36, Q37]\n● Mahatma Gandhi ne Rabindranath ko 'The Great Sentinel' kaha tha — Gandhi maante the ki Tagore ne\nfreedom struggle ko moral support diya. [Q38]\n●\n Trap: Rabindranath Tagore Swadeshi Movement ke ECONOMIC aspects (jaise foreign clothes\n⚠️\njalana) ke favour mein NAHI the — unhone iske negative side-effects apne novel 'Ghare Baire' mein\ndikhaye. [Q39]\n● Rabindranath Tagore 70 saal ki age mein ek great painter ki tarah ubhre — 1930 mein Europe, Russia\naur USA mein apne paintings exhibit ki. [Q85]\n27. Ras Behari Bose's Rallying Statement\n● 'Avenge the blood of Indian Martyrs. Use your sword to liberate...' — ye powerful statement\nrevolutionary Ras Behari Bose ne diya tha. [Q40]\n28. 'Jai Jawan Jai Kisan' — Lal Bahadur Shastri\n● 'Jai Jawan Jai Kisan' slogan tatkaleen Prime Minister Lal Bahadur Shastri ne 1965 mein, Ramlila\nMaidan (Delhi) mein diya tha. [Q41]\n29. The Gregorian Calendar\n● Present-day calendar 'Gregorian Calendar' par based hai — worldwide use hota hai. [Q42]\n30. Bhartiya Kisan Sangh\n●\n Disputed: 'Bhartiya Kisan Sangh' 4 March 1979 ko, Kota (Rajasthan) mein, Dattopant Thengdi ne\n⚠️\nestablish ki thi — 1979 saal diye gaye options mein na hone ki wajah se ye question disputed hai. [Q43]\n31. Gandhi's Quit India Quotes\n● 'Freedom is almost within reach, we have to seize it' — ye statement Mahatma Gandhi ne, Quit India\nMovement (9 August 1942) ke waqt diya, saath hi 'Do or Die' ka slogan bhi. [Q44]\n32. Subhash Bose on Gandhi's Leadership","● 'India's salvation will not be achieved under his leadership' — ye statement Subhash Chandra Bose ne\napni book 'The Indian Struggle' mein, Gandhiji ke baare mein likha tha. [Q45]\n33. Assertion-Reason — Nationalist Leaders & 'Providence'\n● Assertion-Reason: Early nationalist leaders British rule ko 'Providence' (ishwar-nirdharit) tool maante\nthe, jo modernization laayegi (sahi Assertion) — unki criticism sirf 'Un-British rule' tak limited thi (sahi\nReason bhi) — lekin official answer key ke mutabik Reason, Assertion ka sahi explanation NAHI deta.\n[Q46]\n34. Nehru's Statement on Agriculture\n● 'Everything else can wait, but not agriculture' — ye statement Jawaharlal Nehru ne Independence ke\nbaad kaha tha. [Q47]\n35. The First Cloth Mill in Bombay\n● Pehla Indian cotton cloth mill 1818 mein, Fort Gloaster (Kolkata) mein bana tha lekin fail ho gaya —\npehli successful modern cloth mill 1854 mein Bombay mein, Parsi cotton merchant Cowaszee\nNanabhoy Davar ne banayi. [Q48]\n36. Dadabhai Naoroji's Statement\n● 'Kings are made for Public; Public is not made for the King' — ye statement Dadabhai Naoroji ('Grand\nOld Man of India') ne diya tha. [Q49]\n37. Boy Scouts Movement — Baden-Powell\n● Robert Baden-Powell ne 1 August 1907 ko Brown Sea Island mein camp lagakar 'Boy Scouts'\nmovement shuru ki — India mein Boy Scouts aur Civil Guides Movement ke founder maane jaate hain\n(India mein scouting 1909 mein, guiding 1911 mein aayi). [Q50]\n38. The Rakhmabai Case (1884)\n● Rakhmabai ek pehli practising women doctors mein se thi colonial India mein — 1884-1888 ke beech\nunke child marriage se related ek landmark legal case (restitution of conjugal rights, consent age) chala,\njisse 'Age of Consent Act' (1891) bani. [Q51]\n39. Freedom Struggle — Incorrect Statement Check","●\n Trap: 1931 ke Karachi Session mein Congress ne Gandhi-Irwin Pact ka VIRODH NAHI kiya — ulta\n⚠️\nise APPROVE kiya tha (5 March 1931 mein sign hui thi). [Q52]\n40. Statements About Jawaharlal Nehru — All Incorrect\n●\n Trap: Jawaharlal Nehru se related sabhi diye gaye statements GALAT hain — 1947 mein J.B.\n⚠️\nKripalani Congress President the (Nehru NAHI), Rajendra Prasad permanent Constituent Assembly\nPresident the, aur UP ke pehle Congress Ministry mein Nehru shaamil NAHI the (Govind Ballabh Pant\nChief Minister the). [Q53]\n41. Nehru's Socialist-Republican Statement\n● 'I am a socialist and a republican and do not believe in Kings and Princes' — ye statement Jawaharlal\nNehru ne diya tha. [Q54]\n42. Nehru — 'High Priest of Communism' & His Biographer\n● Jawaharlal Nehru ko 'High Priest of Communism in India' kaha gaya tha — United Provinces ke\nPublicity Department ke ek pamphlet mein ('Communistic Likes and Dislikes'), unke socialistic views ko\nconfuse karne wale propaganda ki tarah. [Q55]\n● Nehru socialism ke champion bane — 1933 mein British rule, Princely states, Landlordism aur\nCapitalism khatam karna chahte the, 1927 mein Soviet Union visit se inspire hokar. [Q56]\n● Frank Moraes, Jawaharlal Nehru ke biographer the. [Q57]\n43. Ambabai — Woman Freedom Fighter\n● Ambabai, ek woman freedom fighter, purane Mysore State (aaj Karnataka) se belong karti thi — unhone\nSalt Satyagraha mein Udipi mein foreign cloth-liquor shops picket ki. [Q58]\n44. The 'Sarabandi Campaign' — Sardar Patel\n● 'Sarabandi' (No-tax) Campaign, Bardoli (Gujarat) mein, Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel ne lead ki thi. [Q59]\n45. The Origin of the Word 'Boycott'\n● 'Boycott' word Captain Charles C. Boycott (Irish land agent) ke naam se derived hai — unhi ke against\n1880 mein ye ek political weapon ki tarah pehli baar use hua. [Q60]","46. N.M. Joshi — India at the ILO\n● N.M. Joshi ko Indian Government ne 1919 Washington ILO summit mein labourers ka representative\nbanakar bheja tha — B.P. Wadia unke advisor the. [Q61]\n47. Statements — Arya Samaj, Al-Hilal & Presidency College\n● Statement check: Arya Samaj 1875 mein Dayananda Saraswati ne bani (sahi), 'Al Hilal' Abul Kalam\nAzad ne 1912 mein publish ki (sahi) — Lala Lajpat Rai 'The People' se associate NAHI the (galat) —\nPresidency College Ram Mohan Roy-David Hare ne 1817 mein banaya (sahi). [Q62]\n48. Chronology — 'Kesari' to 'Al Hilal'\n● Chronological order: Kesari ki shuruat (1881) → Khudiram Bose ki execution (1908) → Curzon Wyllie ki\nassassination (1909) → Al Hilal ki shuruat (1912). [Q63]\n49. Third Event in Chronological Order — Dandi March\n● Chronological order: Champaran Movement (1917) → Non-Cooperation Movement (1920-22) → Dandi\nMarch (1930, 3rd) → Quit India Movement (1942). [Q64]\n50. Statements — Gandhi & Colonial Rule\n● Statement check: Gandhi ne Viceroy Chelmsford se negotiate karke indentured labour system July\n1917 mein ban karwaya (sahi) — Salt March (1930) ke baad INC ko illegal declare kiya gaya aur\nleaders arrest hue (sahi) — lekin Gandhi ne WWI mein army recruitment ka virodh NAHI kiya, unhone\nactually support kiya tha (galat). [Q65]\n51. Aruna Asaf Ali's Post-1947 Contribution\n● Aruna Asaf Ali ne 1947 ke baad politics mein sabse zyada contribute kiya — left socialist group se juri,\naur 1958 mein Delhi ki pehli Mayor bani. [Q66]\n52. Sardar Patel's Statement on Bihar Riots\n● 'Agar hum Bihar ke logo aur unki Government ko violence-anarchy ke saamne asuraksit chhod dein, to\nye humari galti hogi' — ye statement Sardar Patel ne 1946 mein, Bihar ke violent riots ke context mein\ndiya tha. [Q67]","53. First Demand for 'Complete Independence' — Hasrat Mohani\n● Maulana Hasrat Mohani ne 1921 mein pehli baar 'Complete Independence' (Poorna Swaraj) ki demand\nki — 1921 ke Ahmedabad Congress Session mein. [Q68]\n54. Mountbatten on Jinnah's Role in Partition\n● Lord Mountbatten (Viceroy 1947-48) ne Muhammad Ali Jinnah ko India ke partition ke liye sabse zyada\nresponsible bataya. [Q69]\n55. Aga Khan — The All Parties Muslim Conference\n● Aga Khan (Maulana Sultan Mohammed Shah) ne, Delhi mein, late December 1928-January 1929 mein\nhui 'All Parties Muslim Conference' ki presidency ki — Muslims ke liye separate electorates ki demand\nke liye banayi gayi thi. [Q70]\n56. The Hindu Mahasabha — Banaras Session (1923)\n● August 1923 ke 'Banaras Session' (Hindu Mahasabha) ki presidency Pandit Madan Mohan Malviya ne\nki — lagbhag 1500 delegates (Hindus, Jains, Sikhs, Parsis samet) attend hue. [Q71]\n57. Sachchidananda Sinha — 'Creator of Modern Bihar'\n● Sachchidananda Sinha ko 'Creator of Modern Bihar' maana jaata hai — unhone Bengal Presidency se\nalag ek separate Bihar province ke liye movement lead ki, jo 1912 mein realize hui. [Q72]\n● 'So always with the assent and often to the dictates of the Chamber of Commerce, the Government of\nIndia...' — ye statement Sachchidananda Sinha ne diya tha. [Q229]\n58. Founding Years — CPI & RSS (1925)\n● Communist Party of India (CPI, December 1925, Kanpur) aur Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh (RSS, 27\nSeptember 1925, Nagpur) — dono 1925 mein hi bane the. [Q73]\n59. 'Frontier Gandhi' — Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan\n● Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan ko 'Frontier Gandhi' kehte hain — Mahatma Gandhi ke saath unke close\nassociation aur pacifist tareeko ki wajah se. [Q74, Q75, Q76]","60. The 'Bombay Trimurti'\n● Pherozeshah Mehta, K.T. Telang aur Badruddin Tyabji — 'Bombay Trimurti' kehlaate hain — unhone\nmilkar 1885 mein Bombay Presidency Association banayi. [Q77]\n61. Khudai Khidmatgars — The 'Red Shirts'\n● Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan ne 'Khudai Khidmatgar' (Servants of God) organize ki — jinhe 'Red Shirts' bhi\nkehte the — Civil Disobedience Movement ke dauran non-violence aur freedom struggle ka pledge liya.\n[Q78, Q79]\n62. Dr. B.S. Moonje's Attack on Ambedkar\n● Dr. B.S. Moonje (Hindu nationalist leader) ne 1932 mein, Ambedkar ki separate electorate ki demand ke\nresponse mein, kaha: 'Ambedkar has had his leadership thrust upon him...' [Q80]\n63. History's Role in Creating Nationalism\n● History ki study ne India mein nationalism ki feeling create karne mein har tarike se madad ki — British\nrule ke against struggle ke liye logo ko urge kiya, backwardness ki British narrative ko counter kiya, aur\nIndia ke glorious past ko highlight kiya. [Q81]\n64. Tripura & the Freedom Movement\n● Tripura native state 20th century ki shuruat mein freedom movement mein involve hui — British ke\npressure mein, Bengal ke revolutionaries ne Tripura mein sharan li thi. [Q82]\n65. Rajendra Prasad — From Bihar\n● Dr. Rajendra Prasad, 3 December 1884 ko, Ziradei village (Siwan district, Bihar) mein paida hue the.\n[Q83]\n66. Women Saint Daya Bai\n● Women Saint Daya Bai, Saint Charandas ki disciple thi — unhone 'Dayabodh' naam ki book likhi. [Q84]\n67. St. Francis Xavier","● Statement check: St. Francis Xavier, Jesuit order ke founding members mein se ek the — unki mrityu 3\nDecember 1552 ko Shangchuan Island (China) mein hui, Goa mein NAHI (isliye galat statement). [Q86]\n68. Jagat Narain Lal — Hazaribagh Jail\n● Jagat Narain Lal ko freedom struggle ke dauran Hazaribagh Jail bheja gaya tha. [Q87]\n69. The Aga Khan Palace Samadhis\n● Kasturba Gandhi aur Mahadev Desai ki Samadhis, Aga Khan Palace (Pune) ke premises mein hain.\n[Q88, Q89]\n70. The Official History of Congress — Pattabhi Sitaramayya\n● Dr. Pattabhi Sitaramayya, Congress ki official history ke author the. [Q90]\n71. The Whitley Commission\n● Colonial period mein, 'Whitley Commission' ka purpose tha British India ke industrial undertakings-\nplantations mein labour ki existing conditions par report dena aur recommendations dena. [Q91]\n72. Foreign Commentators on Colonial India\n● Katherine Mayo, Aldous Huxley, Charles Andrews aur William Digby — sabhi ne British rule ke dauran\nIndia ki condition par commentaries likhi. [Q92]\n73. The Bengal Famine of 1943\n● 1943 ke Bengal Famine mein lagbhag 3 million log maare gaye. [Q93]\n74. Non-Alignment\n● Global peace aur cooperation establish karne ke liye, 'Non-Alignment' ka concept introduce kiya gaya\ntha. [Q94]\n75. Goa — Under Portuguese Control After Independence","● 15 August 1947 ke baad, Goa Portuguese control mein raha — 1961 mein 'Operation Vijay' ke through\nliberate hua. Portuguese hi ekmatra colonial power thi jinke against azaadi ki ladai independence ke\nbaad bhi continue rahi. [Q95, Q96]\n76. Nehru — NOT Influenced by German Nationalism\n●\n Trap: Jawaharlal Nehru 'German Nationalism' se influenced NAHI the — unhone Nazism aur\n⚠️\nFascism ka strongly virodh kiya. [Q97]\n77. Dominant Castes in Pre-Independence Bihar\n●\n Trap: Pre-independence Bihar mein Bhumihar, Rajput aur Kayastha dominant castes thi — Kurmi in\n⚠️\nmein SHAAMIL NAHI thi. [Q98]\n78. Shimla Conference & the Royal Indian Navy Revolt\n● Statement check: Shimla Conference (1945) ke waqt Lord Wavell Viceroy the, Mountbatten NAHI (galat\nstatement) — Royal Indian Navy revolt 18 February 1946 ko, Bombay aur Karachi mein shuru hui (sahi\nstatement). [Q99]\n79. Statements — Vidyasagar & Bethune School\n● Statement check: Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar, Bethune School ke first secretary the (sahi), Bankim\nChandra Calcutta University ke pehle 2 graduates mein se ek the (1858, sahi) — lekin Sati ban 1829\nmein Ram Mohan Roy ke campaign se hui, Keshav Chandra Sen se NAHI (galat). [Q100]\n80. Earliest Event — Neeldarpan\n● Sabse pehle hua event: Dinabandhu Mitra ne 'Neeldarpan' likhi (1860) — Satyendra Nath Tagore ka\nICS pass karna (1864), Arya Samaj ki sthapna (1875), aur 'Anandmath' likhi jaana (1880) baad mein\nhue. [Q101]\n81. First Indian in the British Parliament\n● Lal Mohan Ghose (1885) British House of Commons election contest karne wale pehle Indian the —\nlekin Dadabhai Naoroji pehle Indian the jo actually elect hue (1892, Liberal Party ticket par, Central\nFinsbury se). [Q102, Q103]\n● Indirect election ki practice India mein Indian Councils Act, 1892 ke through launch hui. [Q104]","82. The Deoband Scholar — Abul Kalam Azad\n● Abul Kalam Azad, Deoband movement se related ek scholar the, jinhone freedom movement mein\nsignificant role play kiya — 1940-1946 tak Congress President rahe aur 'India Wins Freedom' likhi.\n[Q105]\n83. Chronology — Jallianwala Report to the Calcutta Session (1920)\n● Chronological order: Jallianwala Bagh Report submission (25 March 1920) → Turkey ke saath Peace\nTerms ki announcement (14 May 1920) → B.G. Tilak ki demise (1 August 1920) → INC ka Special\nSession, Calcutta (4-9 September 1920). [Q107]\n84. Independent India's First Industrial Policy\n● Independent India ki pehli Industrial Policy 6 April 1948 ko announce hui — India ke liye 'mixed\neconomy' ka concept introduce kiya, industries ko public-private sectors mein baata. [Q108]\n85. The First Communist Government — Kerala\n● India ki pehli Communist Government 1957 mein Kerala mein establish hui — E.M.S. Namboodiripad ki\nleadership mein. [Q109, Q110]\n86. National Observance Days\n● India mein 'Teacher's Day' 5 September ko manaya jaata hai — Dr. Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan ki birth\nanniversary ki yaad mein. [Q111]\n● 'National Press Day' 16 November ko manaya jaata hai. [Q112]\n● Match: World Population Day → 11 July; International Youth Day → 12 August; National Sports Day →\n29 August; World Literacy Day → 8 September. [Q113]\n● 'Civil Service Day' 21 April ko celebrate hota hai — pehla function 21 April 2006 ko New Delhi mein hua.\n[Q114]\n● 'Valentine Day' har saal 14 February ko celebrate hota hai. [Q115]\n87. Chronology — Air India to Goa (Post-Independence)\n● Chronological order: Air India nationalise hui (1953) → Imperial Bank ka naam SBI hua (July 1955) →\nKerala mein first communist government (April 1957) → Goa India ka hissa bana (1961). [Q116]","88. Nehru vs Gandhi — Heavy Industrialization\n● Gandhi small-cottage industries ke development par zor dete the — Nehru 'heavy industrialization' ka\nsupport karte the. [Q117]\n89. Gandhi's Statement at the Karachi Session (1931)\n● 'Gandhi may die, but Gandhism will remain' — ye statement Gandhi ne March 1931 ke Karachi Session\nmein diya tha. [Q118]\n90. The 'Struggle-Truce-Struggle' (S-T-S) Strategy\n●\n Disputed: 'Struggle-Truce-Struggle' (S-T-S) political strategy Mahatma Gandhi ne use ki — BPSC ne\n⚠️\n\nis question ko delete kar diya, kyunki ye strategy Civil Disobedience Movement se sabse prominently\nassociate maani jaati hai, jo diye gaye options se match nahi karti. [Q119]\n91. The C.R. Formula\n● C. Rajagopalachari ne July 1944 mein, Gandhi ki approval se, Muslim League aur INC ke beech\npolitical deadlock khatam karne ka plan diya — 'C.R. Formula' kehlaayi, Jinnah ne isse reject kiya.\n[Q120]\n92. Disputed — Organizations' Founding Years\n●\n Disputed: All India Women's Conference 1927 mein bani (1926 NAHI), All India Depressed Classes\n⚠️\nAssociation 1926 mein M.C. Raja ne banayi, Bombay Social Reform Association 1903 mein bani, aur\nIndian National Social Conference M.G. Ranade ne 1887 mein banayi — multiple options galat matched\nhone ki wajah se ye question disputed hai. [Q121]\n93. Gandhi's Key Milestones — Match List\n● Match: Yerwada Prison → Civil Disobedience Movement; Fast unto death → Communal Award ke\nagainst; Black flags dikhaye gaye Karachi jaate waqt → Gandhi-Irwin Pact endorse karne ke liye;\n'Defeat more mine than theirs' (Sitaramayya) → 1939 ka Congress Crisis (Tripuri). [Q122]\n94. Chronology — Constitutional Reforms & Acts\n● Chronological order (Non-cooperation to Quit India): Non-cooperation Movement (1920-22) → Simon\nCommission (1927-28) → Nehru Report (1928) → Quit India Movement (1942). [Q123]","● Sequence: Rowlatt Act (1919) → Simon Commission (1927) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (1931) — Home Rule\nMovement (1916) sabse pehle. [Q142]\n● Sequence: Partition of Bengal (1905) → Lucknow Pact (1916) → Rowlatt Act (March 1919) →\nIntroduction of Dyarchy (December 1919, GoI Act 1919). [Q145]\n● Sequence: Passing of Rowlatt Bill (18 March 1919) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919) →\nAmritsar Session of INC (26-30 December 1919) → B.G. Tilak ki demise (1 August 1920). [Q150]\n● Sequence: Rowlatt Act (18 March 1919) → Rowlatt Satyagraha (6 April 1919) → Amritsar Session (Dec\n1919) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919). [Q155]\n● Sequence: Home Rule Movement (1916) → Champaran Satyagraha (1917) → Rowlatt Satyagraha\n(April 1919) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919). [Q156]\n● Match: Indian Council Act 1909 → Morley-Minto Reform; GoI Act 1919 → Montague-Chelmsford\nReform; GoI Act 1935 → Simon Commission Report/Joint Select Committee; Indian Independence Act\n1947 → Mountbatten Plan. [Q166]\n● Sequence: Ban on Sati (1829) → Wood's Despatch (1854) → Vernacular Press Act (1878) → Rowlatt\nAct (1919). [Q189]\n● Match: MacDonald → Communal Award (1932); Linlithgow → August Offer (1940); Dalhousie →\nDoctrine of Lapse; Chelmsford → Dyarchy (GoI Act 1919). [Q204]\n● Sequence: Wood's Despatch (19 July 1854) → Hunter Commission (1882, Ripon) → Sadler\nCommission (1917) → Sargeant Plan (1944). [Q205]\n●\n Trap: Ahom Rebellion 1828 mein hui thi, 1815 mein NAHI — Santhal (1855-56), Kol (1831-32) aur\n⚠️\nKhasi (1829-33) sahi matched hain. [Q207]\n● Match: 1883 → First National Conference (Calcutta); 1906 → Muslim League ki foundation (Dhaka);\n1927 → All India States People Conference; 1932 → Ramsay MacDonald ne Communal Award\nannounce ki (Whitehall se). [Q159]\n● Match: Morley-Minto Reform (1909) → Communal Electorates; Simon Commission (1927) → Nation-\nwide Movement; Chauri-Chaura (1922) → Non-cooperation ki withdrawal; Dandi March (1930) → Illegal\nsalt manufacturing. [Q160]\n●\n Trap: Communal Award 1932 mein announce hui thi, 1933 mein NAHI — Ramsay MacDonald ne 16\n⚠️\n\nAugust 1932 ko diya. [Q162]\n● Match: Indian Council Act 1909 → Lord Minto (Morley-Minto); GoI Act 1919 → Chelmsford; GoI Act\n1935 → Simon Commission; Indian Independence Act 1947 → Mountbatten. [Q217]\n95. Chronology — Early Movements (1905-1916)\n● Sequence: Regulating Act (1773) → Partition of Bengal (1905) → Muslim League ki sthapna (1906) →\nSurat split (1907). [Q140]\n● Match: Home Rule League → Lokmanya Tilak (1916); Swaraj Party → Chittaranjan Das (1923);\nNationalist Party → Madan Mohan Malviya; National Liberal Federation → Tej Bahadur Sapru. [Q187]\n● Sequence: Surat Split (1907) → Muslim League ki foundation (Dhaka, 1906 — pehle) → Home Rule\nMovement (1916) → Kheda Satyagraha (1918). [Q161]","● Sequence: Partition of Bengal declare hui (20 July 1905) → Swadeshi Movement announce hui (7\nAugust 1905) → Swaraj ko Congress ka goal accept kiya gaya (December 1906, Calcutta) → Surat Split\n(1907). [Q225]\n● Sequence: Regulating Act, Partition of Bengal, Muslim League ki sthapna, Surat Split — sabhi 20th\ncentury ki shuruaat ke pehle ke events hain, jo colonial governance ke evolution ko dikhate hain. [Q184]\n● Sequence: Swadeshi Movement (1905) → Home Rule Movement (1916) → Non-cooperation (1920) →\nCivil Disobedience (1930). [Q222]\n● Sequence: Swadeshi Movement se lekar Civil Disobedience Movement tak ke important milestones ek\nchain mein connect hote hain — har movement pichle se seekh leta hai. [Q177]\n96. Chronology — Rowlatt to Jallianwala Bagh (Multiple Sequences)\n● Sequence: Champaran Satyagraha (1917) → Rowlatt Satyagraha (April 1919) → Jallianwala Bagh\nMassacre (13 April 1919) → Chauri-Chaura Episode (4 Feb 1922). [Q154]\n● Sequence: Home Rule Movement (1916) → Champaran Satyagraha (1917) → Rowlatt Satyagraha\n(April 1919) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919). [Q153]\n● Sequence: Jallianwala Bagh Tragedy (13 April 1919) → Formation of Swaraj Party (1923) → Naujawan\nBharat Sabha ki foundation (March 1926) → Dandi March (1930). [Q157]\n● Sequence: Lucknow Pact (1916) → Champaran Satyagraha (1917) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13\nApril 1919) → Khilafat Movement (October 1919). [Q146]\n● Sequence: Lucknow Pact (Dec 1916) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919) → Tilak ki death (1\nAug 1920) → Swaraj Party ki formation (1923). [Q147]\n● Sequence: Champaran Movement (1917) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919) → Moplah\nMovement (1921) → Chauri-Chaura Incident (4 Feb 1922). [Q197, Q232]\n● Sequence: Champaran (1917) → Jallianwala Bagh (1919) → Non-cooperation Movement (1920) →\nCivil Disobedience Movement (1930). [Q186]\n● Sequence: Home Rule Movement (1916) → Non-Cooperation Movement (1920-22) → Civil\nDisobedience Movement (1930) → Quit India Movement (1942). [Q180]\n● Sequence: Champaran Satyagraha (I) → Non-Cooperation Movement (II) → Quit India Movement (IV)\n→ Civil Disobedience Movement (III) is one order variant. [Q141]\n97. Chronology — Lahore Session, Communal Award & Poona Pact\n● Sequence: Simon Commission (arrived 1928) → Dandi March (March-April 1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact\n(5 March 1931) → Poona Pact (24 September 1932). [Q126]\n● Sequence: Dandi Yatra (12 March 1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Communal Award (16\nAugust 1932) → Poona Pact (24 September 1932). [Q127]\n● Sequence: Chauri-Chaura Incident (1922) → Dandi March (1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (March 1931) →\nCommunal Award (August 1932) — Communal Award sabse aakhri hua. [Q124]","● Sequence: Complete Independence Resolution (31 Dec 1929) → Purna Swaraj Day (26 Jan 1930) →\nDandi March (12 March 1930) → Second Round Table Conference (7 Sept 1931). [Q208]\n● Sequence: Nehru Report (1928) → Civil Disobedience Movement (1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March\n1931) → Poona Pact (1932). [Q198]\n● Sequence: Complete National Independence ki declaration (31 December 1929) → Civil Disobedience\nCampaign (6 April 1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Agreement (5 March 1931) → Poona Pact (24 Sept 1932).\n[Q199]\n● Sequence: Nehru Report (1928) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Second Round Table\nConference (Sept-Dec 1931) → Communal Award (16 August 1932). [Q200]\n● Sequence: Communal Award (16 August 1932) → Poona Pact (24 September 1932) → Third Round\nTable Conference (17 Nov-24 Dec 1932) → August Offer (1940). [Q195]\n● Sequence: Martyrdom of Chandra Shekhar Azad (27 Feb 1931) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) →\nExecution of Bhagat Singh-Sukhdev-Rajguru (23 March 1931) → Karachi Session of INC (29-31 March\n1931). [Q245]\n● Sequence: Lahore Session of Congress (December 1929) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) →\nBhagat Singh-Sukhdev-Rajguru ki execution (23 March 1931) → Karachi Session of Congress (29-31\nMarch 1931). [Q246]\n● Simon Commission (2), Poona Pact (4), Cripps Mission (3), Cabinet Mission (1) — is sequence mein\narrange hue. [Q219]\n98. Chronology — August Offer to Cabinet Mission (1940-1946)\n● Sequence: Congress Ministries ka resignation (October 1939) → Ramgarh Congress Session (March\n1940) → Linlithgow ka August Offer (August 1940) → Cripps Mission (March 1942). [Q129]\n● Sequence: August Offer (August 1940) → Cripps Mission (March 1942) → C.R. Formula (July 1944) →\nWavell Plan (1945). [Q171]\n● Sequence: August Offer (1940) → Cripps Mission (March 1942) → Quit India Movement (August 1942)\n→ Desai-Liaquat Pact (1945). [Q172]\n● Sequence: Nehru Report (1928) → August Offer (1940) → Cripps Mission (1942) → Wavell Plan\n(1945). [Q194, Q202]\n● Cripps Mission (March 1942) pehle event thi — Quit India Resolution (August 1942), Lord Wavell ka\nViceroy ki tarah aana (October 1943), aur Cabinet Mission ka aana (March 1946) baad mein hue. [Q170]\n● Sequence: August Offer (1940) → Cripps Mission (1942) → Wavell Plan (1945) → Cabinet Mission Plan\n(1946). [Q193]\n● Sequence: C.R. Formula (1944) → Wavell Plan (1945) → Cabinet Mission Plan (1946) → Mountbatten\nPlan (1947). [Q201]\n● Sequence: Jinnah ne Shimla Conference todi (14 July 1945) → Cabinet Mission ka aana (24 March\n1946) → Muslim League ka Direct Action (16 August 1946) → Interim Government ki formation (2\nSeptember 1946). [Q128]\n● Sequence: UK Parliamentary Delegation ka aana (January 1946) → Royal Indian Navy Revolt\n(February 1946) → Cabinet Mission ka aana (March 1946) → Interim Government ki formation\n(September 1946). [Q168]","● Match: GoI Act 1935; Cripps Proposals (1942); August Offer (1940); Wavell Plan (1945) — inke sahi\ncorresponding years/sequences. [Q169]\n● Sequence: C.R. Formula (July 1944) → Gandhi-Jinnah Dialogue (September 1944) → Wavell Plan\n(June 1945) → Cabinet Mission (March 1946). [Q210]\n● Sequence: Cripps Mission (March 1942) → Individual Satyagraha (1940, waapas count karke pehle) →\nQuit India Movement (August 1942) — variant sequence with Civil Disobedience (1930) leading. [Q218]\n● Sequence: Simon Commission (arrived Feb 1928) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Cripps\nMission (March 1942) → Partition of the country (midnight 14-15 August 1947). [Q182]\n● Sequence: Cripps Mission (March 1942), August Offer (1940), Nehru Report (1928), Wavell Plan (1945)\n— sahi order Nehru Report → August Offer → Cripps Mission → Wavell Plan hai. [Q192]\n● Sequence: Poona Pact (1932) → Quit India Movement (9 August 1942) → Simla Conference (25 June\n1945) → Cabinet Mission (24 March 1946 ko arrive hui). [Q223]\n● Sequence: Second Round Table Conference (7 Sept-1 Dec 1931) → Quit India Movement (9 August\n1942) → Royal Indian Navy mein mutiny (18-23 February 1946). [Q224]\n● 'Deepavali Declaration' (31 October 1929, Viceroy Lord Irwin) — India ke liye Dominion Status promise\nkarne se related thi. [Q173]\n99. Match Lists — Movements & Their Leaders/Founders\n● Match: Azad Muslim Conference → Allah Baksh; Khaksar Party → Allama Mashriqui; Khudai\nKhidmatgar → Abdul Gaffar Khan; Krishak Praja Party → Fazlul Haq. [Q131]\n● Match: Bardoli Satyagraha → Sardar Patel (1928); Champaran Satyagraha → Gandhi (1917); Kuka\nMovement → Ram Singh; Lal Kurti Movement → Gaffar Khan. [Q132]\n●\n Disputed: Awadh Kisan Sabha, JL Nehru-Baba Ram Chandra ke efforts se bani; All India Kisan\n⚠️\nSabha (1936) mein Narendra Dev jaise prominent members the, Sahajanand Saraswati ne shuru ki —\nquestion ke sabhi options sahi lagne ki wajah se disputed hai. [Q133]\n●\n Disputed: Khilafat Movement → Ali Brothers; Home Rule Movement → Tilak; Civil Disobedience\n⚠️\nMovement → Khan Brothers;\n B.R. Ambedkar Quit India Movement mein participate NAHI hue the\n⚠️\n(Aruna Asaf Ali associate thi) — flawed options ki wajah se disputed hai. [Q134]\n●\n Trap: 'M.A. Jinnah - Khilafat Movement' galat match hai — Jinnah ne Khilafat Movement mein\n⚠️\nGandhi ki ninda ki thi aur is se door rahe, Ali Brothers (Shaukat-Muhammad) ne movement start ki thi.\n[Q135]\n● Match: Vinoba Bhave → Individual Satyagraha; B.G. Tilak → Home Rule Movement; Aruna Asaf Ali →\nQuit India Movement; Sarojini Naidu → Dharsana Raid. [Q136]\n● Sahi pair: 'C.R. Das - Deshbandhu' — Vinoba Bhave pehle Individual Satyagrahi the (doosre NAHI),\nRash Behari Ghosh 1907 Surat Session ke President the, Shyamji Krishna Verma ne India House\nLondon mein banayi thi (Paris mein NAHI). [Q137]\n● Match: Home Rule Movement (1916) → Annie Besant; Bardoli Satyagraha (1928) → Sardar Patel; Non-\nCooperation Movement (1920) → M.K. Gandhi; Swaraj Party (1923) → C.R. Das. [Q138]\n● Match: Mahatma Gandhi → Dandi March; Jawaharlal Nehru → Complete Independence Demand\n(Lahore Session); Khan Abdul Gaffar Khan → Red Shirt Movement; Vallabhbhai Patel → Bardoli\nSatyagraha. [Q139]","● Match: Complete Independence Resolution (31 Dec 1929, Congress) → Purna Swaraj Day (26 Jan\n1930) → Dandi March start (12 March 1930) → Second Round Table Conference (7 Sept 1931). [Q209]\n● Match: Annie Besant → Home Rule Movement (Sept 1916); Rajendra Prasad → Champaran\nSatyagraha (1917); Jawaharlal Nehru → Lahore Session (1929); Ambika Charan Majumdar → Lucknow\nSession (1916). [Q167]\n● Match: Madan Mohan Malviya → BHU founder; Motilal Nehru → Swaraj Party (1923); Annie Besant →\nHome Rule League (1916); Gopal Krishna Gokhale → Servants of India Society (1905). [Q212]\n● Match: Khaksars → Inayatullah Mashriqui; Socialist Party → Jayaprakash Narayan; Independent\nLabour Party → B.R. Ambedkar; Forward Bloc → Subhas Chandra Bose. [Q213]\n●\n Trap: Ghadar Party — Lala Lajpat Rai se NAHI, Sohan Singh Bhakna-Lala Hardayal ne San\n⚠️\nFrancisco (USA) mein 1913 mein banayi thi. [Q214]\n● Match: Subhash Chandra Bose → Haripura Session of INC; Vallabhbhai Patel → Operation Polo; Iqbal\n→ Allahabad Session of Muslim League (1930); Batukeshwar Dutt → Central Assembly mein bomb\n(Bhagat Singh ke saath). [Q247]\n100. Match Lists & Not-Correctly-Matched Traps — Various Pairs\n●\n Trap: 'Bal Gangadhar Tilak — Satya Shodhak Sabha' galat match hai — Satya Shodhak Samaj\n⚠️\n(1873) Jyotiba Phule ne banayi thi. [Q158]\n●\n Trap: 'Bombay Chronicle — Gopal Krishna Gokhale' galat match hai — Bombay Chronicle\n⚠️\nPherozeshah Mehta ne 1910 mein publish ki thi. [Q206]\n● Statement check: Asaf Ali ne 1946 mein Railway Ministry sambhali (sahi), Ancient Monuments\nPreservation Act 1904 mein Curzon ne pass ki (sahi) — lekin Haripura Session (1938) ki presidency\nSubhash Chandra Bose ne ki, C.R. Das ne NAHI (galat) — Swami Shraddhanand ne Rowlatt Act ke\nagainst no-tax campaign suggest ki (sahi). [Q143]\n● Match: Rani Durgavati → Garha Katanga (Gara Mandal); Ahilya Bai → Holkar State; Lakshmi Bai →\nJhansi; Razia Sultan → Delhi. [Q144]\n●\n Trap: 'Governor-General of Bengal jab Pitt's India Act pass hui — Lord Minto' galat hai — us waqt\n⚠️\nWarren Hastings the. [Q165]\n● Statement check: Theodore Beck M.A.O. College Aligarh ke pehle principal the (sahi), Ilbert Bill 1884\nmein Ripon ke time pass hui (sahi), Pherozeshah Mehta INC ke founder member the (sahi) — lekin\nBadruddin Tyabji Muslim League se NAHI, Congress ke pehle Muslim President (1887) the (galat).\n[Q183]\n● Swadeshi Movement se lekar Movements — women ne har major national movement (Swadeshi, Home\nRule, Non-Cooperation, Civil Disobedience) mein active participate kiya, gharelu seclusion se bahar\naakar. [Q185]\n● Statement check: Champaran Satyagraha (1917) mein Rajendra Prasad-J.B. Kripalani associate the\n(sahi) — Ahmedabad Mill Workers Satyagraha Anusuya Ben ke saath thi, Morarji Desai ke NAHI (galat)\n— Kheda Satyagraha Indulal Yagnik-Vallabhbhai Patel ke saath launch hui (sahi). [Q220]\n●\n Trap: 'Suresh Tendulkar - Political Scientist' galat match hai — Suresh Tendulkar ek economist the.\n⚠️\n[Q236]","●\n Trap: 'The National Song Vande Mataram poori tarah Bengali mein compose hui' — ye statement\n⚠️\ngalat hai — Bankim Chandra Chatterjee ne ise Bengali AUR Sanskrit — dono mein compose kiya, apne\nnovel 'Anand Math' mein. [Q238]\n101. The Trade Disputes Act, 1929\n● 'Trade Disputes Act, 1929' ne tribunals ka system banaya (Board of Conciliation, Court of Inquiry) — aur\npublicly useful services mein bina prior notice ke strikes-lockouts ko ban kiya. [Q216]\n102. Nehru's Political Career — Terms & Statements\n● Statement check: Nehru 1952, 1957, 1962 mein elections jeetkar 4th term mein Prime Minister the\n(1964 mein mrityu tak, sahi statement) — wo Phulpur constituency represent karte the, Rae Bareilly\nNAHI (galat) — Morarji Desai March 1977 mein first Non-Congress PM (Janata Party) bane (sahi).\n[Q233]\n● Assertion-Reason: Nehru ka Upanishads ke prati koi reverence NAHI tha — ye Assertion GALAT hai\n(unka Upanishads mein bahut vishwas tha) — Reason sahi hai ki wo modern India ke 'father of science'\nmane jaate the, scientific point of view rakhte the. [Q226]\n103. Quotes — Attlee, Cripps\n● British PM Clement Attlee ne kaha tha ki 'Imperialism is dead as Dodo' (extinct bird ki tarah). [Q227]\n● 'Here is a revolution taking place and we should move quickly' — ye statement Sir Stafford Cripps ne\ndiya, jo Cripps Mission (1942) aur Cabinet Mission (1946) — dono se juday the. [Q228]\n104. World History — Atomic Bomb & French Revolution\n● Pehla atomic bomb 6 August 1945 ko Hiroshima (Japan) mein giraya gaya — doosra 9 August 1945 ko\nNagasaki mein. [Q230]\n● French Revolution 1789 mein shuru hui — feudalism, class privilege, autocracy ke against middle-class\nlogo ki revolution thi. [Q231]\n105. Disputed Match — Pact/Year & Place\n●\n Disputed: Lucknow Pact (1916) aur Liaquat Ali-Bhulabhai Desai Pact (1945) — dono sahi matched\n⚠️\nhain, isliye Chhattisgarh PSC ki revised answer key ne ye question evaluation se hataya. [Q235]\n●\n Disputed: Bardoli Gujarat mein hai, Chauri-Chaura Gorakhpur (UP) mein, Yerwada Jail Maharashtra\n⚠️\n\nmein — Noakhali (Bangladesh, purana East Bengal) ka exact matching option confusion ki wajah se ye\nquestion disputed hai. [Q237]","106. Post-Independence Foreign Affairs Chronology\n● Sequence: Khrushchev-Bulganin ki India visit (1955) → Dalai Lama ka India bhaagna (1959) → Chou-\nen-Lai ki India visit (April 1960) → Goa ki liberation (1961). [Q239]\n107. The Shimla Agreement (1972)\n● India-Pakistan ke beech 'Shimla Agreement' June-July 1972 mein sign hui — Pakistan President\nZulfiqar Ali Bhutto aur Indian PM Indira Gandhi ke beech, 1971 War ke baad. [Q240]\n108. 'Operation Vijay' — Kargil War\n● 'Operation Vijay' 1999 mein, Pakistan ke against, India ne successfully conduct ki (Kargil War). [Q241]\n109. Kisan Diwas\n● 'Kisan Diwas' 23 December ko manaya jaata hai — ex-PM Chaudhary Charan Singh ki yaad mein.\n[Q242]\n110. Nobel Prize Winners — Match List\n● Match: Rabindranath Tagore → Literature (1913); Amartya Sen → Economics (1998); Chandra Shekhar\n→ Physics/Astrophysics (1983); Vinoo Mankad → Cricket (famous player, Nobel NAHI). [Q243]\n● Rabindranath Tagore, Nobel Prize jeetne wale pehle Indian the — 'Gitanjali' ke liye 1913 mein Literature\nka Nobel — pehle Asian bhi the jinhe Nobel mila. [Q244]\n111. World Political Events — 20th Century\n● China ne 1959 mein Tibet par firmly occupy kiya — jisse Dalai Lama India bhaag aaye, aur Tibet ki\nautonomy khatam ho gayi. [Q259]\n● USSR (Soviet Union) 1991 mein disintegrate hokar 15 alag countries mein baat gaya — Russia iska\nprimary successor state ban gaya (26 December 1991). [Q260]\n● Indo-Pakistan War (December 1971) ke baad Bangladesh ek independent nation ban gaya — 16\nDecember 1971 ko East Pakistan azaad hokar Bangladesh bana. [Q261]\n● Germany, WWII ke baad East-West mein bata hua, 3 October 1990 ko officially reunite hua. [Q262]\n● USA ne WWII mein Japan ke Pearl Harbour attack (December 1941) ke baad militarily participate kiya.\n[Q263]","112. World Leaders — Firsts & Notable Figures\n● George Washington, USA ke pehle President the (1789-1797). [Q264]\n● Richard Nixon (37th US President), Watergate Scandal ki wajah se, resign karne wale ekmatra US\nPresident the (1974 mein). [Q265]\n● Bishop Desmond Tutu, South Africa se juday the — 1980s ke anti-racism movement ke liye world-\nfamous hue, 1984 mein Nobel Peace Prize mila. [Q266]\n113. World History — Paper, Philosophy & the Renaissance\n● Tsai-Lun ko China mein pehli 'real paper' banane ka credit jaata hai — lagbhag 105 AD mein. [Q267]\n● Greek philosopher Plato, Socrates ke disciple the — Aristotle, Plato ke disciple the. [Q268]\n● Italian Renaissance (14th century) ka main cause tha 'freedom to express ideas' — ye modern era ki\nshuruaat maani jaati hai. [Q269]\n114. The 'Kallar' Rebels of Madurai\n● 'Kallar' log, British India ke rebellions ke context mein, Madurai aur uske aas-paas ke South India ke\narea se belong karte the — unhone British control ke against revolt ki. [Q270]\n115. The Indian Councils Act of 1909\n● Act of 1909 (Morley-Minto Reforms) 'Separate Electorate' ke introduction se associate thi. [Q271]\n116. Rama Devi — The Bijolia Peasant Movement\n● Rama Devi Choudhary (Odisha logo dwara 'Maa' kehlaati thi) ne Bijoliya Peasant Movement mein\nparticipate kiya aur arrest hui — 1930 Salt Satyagraha aur Civil Disobedience Movement mein bhi baar-\nbaar arrest hui. [Q272]\n117. Political Party Founding Years — Match List\n● Match: Indian National Congress (1885); Bharatiya Jan Sangh (1951); Communist Party of India (1925);\nA.I.A.D.M.K. (1972). [Q273]\n118. The 'Imperial Gazetteer' — W.W. Hunter","● William Wilson Hunter, ek Indian Civil Services member, ne famous reference work 'The Imperial\nGazetteer of India' compile ki. [Q274]\n119. Gandhi & the Term 'Panchayati Raj'\n● Rural local governments ko 'Panchayati Raj' naam dene ka suggestion Mahatma Gandhi ka tha — unka\nmaanna tha ki villages sirf economically NAHI, politically-administratively bhi independent hone chahiye.\n[Q275]\n120. The Indian National Calendar\n● Indian National Calendar (Saka Samvat) ka pehla mahina 'Chaitra' hai — jo Gregorian Calendar ke\nMarch-April se milta hai; 'Phalgun' aakhri mahina hai. [Q276]\n121. Additional Committees, Chronology & Facts\n●\n Disputed: Dr. B.R. Ambedkar ke baare mein — Baldev Singh India ke pehle Defence Minister the\n⚠️\n(Ambedkar NAHI, statement galat), Bahishkrit Hitkarini Sabha 1924 mein bani (1925 NAHI, statement\ngalat) — koi option perfectly match nahi karta. [Q106]\n● Sequence: Surat Split (1907) → Simon Commission (1928) → Civil Disobedience Movement (1930) →\nKhudai Khidmatgar Movement (1930, closely associated). [Q130]\n●\n Disputed: Swadeshi Movement (1905) → Muslim League ki foundation (1906) → Morley-Minto\n⚠️\nReforms (1909) → Lucknow Pact (1916) — sahi order A-D-C-B hona chahiye tha, diye gaye options\nmein se koi match nahi karta. [Q148]\n●\n Disputed: Rowlatt Satyagraha (6 April 1919) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919) →\n⚠️\nKhilafat Movement (October 1919) → Amritsar Session of INC (26-30 Dec 1919) — sahi order 4,2,1,3\nhona chahiye, koi option perfectly match nahi karta. [Q149]\n● Sequence: Dandi March (12 March-5 April 1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Communal\nAward (16 August 1932) → Poona Pact (24 September 1932). [Q151]\n● Sequence: Civil Disobedience Movement (6 April 1930) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Poona\nPact (24 September 1932) → Cripps Mission (March 1942). [Q152]\n● Sequence: Ferozshah Mehta ki death (5 November 1915) → Jallianwala Bagh Massacre (13 April 1919)\n→ Simon Commission ki appointment (November 1927) → Dandi March (12 March 1930). [Q163]\n● Sequence: Simon Commission ki constitution (1927) → Nehru Report (1928) → Sharda Act (1929) →\nDandi March (1930). [Q164]\n●\n Trap: 'Famine in Western U.P. — 1871-72' galat match hai — actual mein 1860-61 mein hui thi.\n⚠️\n[Q174]\n● Match: Butler Committee (1927) → Princely States-British Govt relationship; Hartog Committee (1929)\n→ Education ka growth; Hunter Inquiry Committee (1919) → Jallianwala Bagh massacre investigation;\nMuddiman Committee (1924) → Dyarchy ka working (Montagu-Chelmsford). [Q175]","●\n Trap: 'Lala Lajpat Rai kabhi INC President elect NAHI hue' — ye statement GALAT hai — wo 1920\n⚠️\nke Calcutta Special Session ke President the. [Q176]\n● Sequence: Kamagatamaru Incident (1914) → Gandhi ka South Africa se India aana (9 January 1915) →\nTilak ki Home Rule League (April 1916). [Q178]\n● Sequence: August Offer (8 August 1940) → Quit India Movement (1942) → INA Trial (November 1945)\n→ Royal Indian Naval Ratings Revolt (February 1946). [Q179]\n● Sequence: Simon Commission ki formation (1927) → Quit India Movement (1942) → INC ki formation\n(1885, sabse pehle) → Morley Minto Reforms (1909) — inka sahi chronological order 3,2,1,4 hai (INC\nformation sabse pehle). [Q181]\n● Match: Separate Electorate ki shuruaat → Morley Minto Reforms (1909); Congress-League Agreement\n→ Lucknow Pact (1916); Communal Award (1932); Deliverance Day (22 December 1939). [Q188]\n● Chronologically pehla event: First Anglo-Sikh War (1845-46) — Santhal Revolt (1855-56), Lord Lytton\nka Delhi Darbar (1877), aur Ilbert Bill Controversy (1883) baad mein hue. [Q190]\n● Sequence: Cripps Plan (1942) → Wavell Plan (1945) → Cabinet Mission Plan (1946) → Mountbatten\nPlan (1947). [Q191]\n● Sequence: Khilafat Movement (October 1919) → Non-Cooperation Movement (1920-22) → Civil\nDisobedience Movement (1930) → Quit India Movement (1942). [Q196]\n● Lord Wavell ne, tatkaleen Viceroy ki tarah, 1945 mein apni 'Wavell Plan' present ki — Shimla mein ek\nconference bulaayi, Interim Government banane jaise proposals ke saath. [Q203]\n● Match: Non-cooperation Movement (1920-22) → Civil Disobedience Movement (1930) → Congress\nMinistries ki formation (1937) → Quit India Movement (1942). [Q211]\n● Sequence: Minto-Morley Reforms (1909) → Montagu-Chelmsford Reforms (1919) → Chauri-Chaura\nOutrage (1922) → Dandi March (1930). [Q215]\n● Sequence: Champaran Satyagraha (1917) → Tilak ki death (1 August 1920) → Dandi March (12 March\n1930) → Shimla Pact/Conference (25 June 1945). [Q221]\n● Sequence: Lucknow Pact (1916) → Gandhi-Irwin Pact (5 March 1931) → Poona Pact (24 September\n1932) → Civil Disobedience Movement ki final withdrawal (1934). [Q234]\n● 'Butler Committee' (1927), Sir Harcourt Butler ki chairmanship mein — Government of India aur Indian\nPrincely States ke beech relationship improve karne ke liye banayi gayi. [Q248]\n● Indian Princely States ke special rights aur privy purse 1971 mein, 26th Constitutional Amendment Act\nse abolish hue. [Q249]\n● Pehli 'All India Socialist Youth Congress' (27 December 1928, Calcutta) ki presidency Jawaharlal Nehru\nne ki. [Q250]\n● 'Hind Mazdoor Sabha' (HMS) December 1948 mein, Calcutta mein, ek trade union conference mein\nbani — Ashok Mehta, T.S. Ramanujam aur G.G. Mehta ismein founders the. [Q251]\n● 'Alipore Central Jail' Kolkata mein situated hai — 1906 mein establish hui, British India ke political\nprisoners yahi qaid rehte the. [Q252]\n● 'Operation Polo' Hyderabad State mein September 1948 mein hui military action ka code name tha —\nIndian Armed Forces ne Hyderabad state invade karke Nizam ko overthrow kiya, Indian Union mein\nannex kiya. [Q253]","● West Bengal ki 'Secretariat Building' ko 'Writer's Building' kehte hain — Kolkata mein hai, originally 1777\nmein East India Company ke junior servants (Writers) ke liye bani thi. [Q254]\n● 'Teen Murti Bhavan' (India ke pehle PM Jawaharlal Nehru ka purana residence) ko 'Prime Ministers\nMuseum' mein convert kiya gaya — PM Narendra Modi ne 14 April 2022 ko inaugurate kiya. [Q255]\n● Karl Marx ne class struggle ka process 'Dialectical Materialism' theory se explain kiya — unke mutabik\nsociety ki history economic causes se determine hoti hai, jo inherently class struggle paida karti hain.\n[Q256]\n●\n Trap: Mother Teresa apni mrityu (5 September 1997) ke waqt Indian citizen NAHI thi — ye\n⚠️\nstatement GALAT hai. [Q257]\n● Mother Teresa dwara establish ki gayi religious organization 'Missionaries of Charity' kehlaati hai. [Q258]\nExam Fusion Prep · examfusionprep.com · Modern History Miscellaneous Full Mind Map"];
